/-! ## Pins as numbers

The recheck path compares addresses with pins, and the kernel has no byte
literals and parses no hex strings cheaply (D17), so a pin is a 256-bit
number: an address's bytes read big-endian. -/

/-- An address as a 256-bit number, its bytes read big-endian. -/
def addrNat (a : Ixon.Address) : Nat := a.hash.data.toList.foldl (fun n b => n * 256 + b.toNat) 0

/-- The address whose number is `n` (`n < 2 ^ 256`): its 32 bytes, big-endian. -/
def addrOfNat (n : Nat) : Ixon.Address :=
  Ixon.Address.ofFn fun i => UInt8.ofNat (n / 256 ^ (31 - i.val) % 256)

